class:: TVonMisesRand
summary:: Triggered random directions on a circle
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/TTruncNormalRand, Classes/TRand, Classes/PanAz

description::

TVonMisesRand chooses random directions around a preferred angle. Concentration controls how tightly the samples gather there: zero spreads them uniformly around the circle. Use it for phase, azimuth, cyclic sequences, and spatial event placement. Unlike link::Classes/TTruncNormalRand::, there is no artificial boundary separating directions near minus pi and plus pi.

The density is proportional to code::exp(kappa * cos(theta-mean))::. The implementation follows D. J. Best and N. I. Fisher, Efficient Simulation of the von Mises Distribution (1979), section 4, link::https://doi.org/10.2307/2346732::. The wrapped-Cauchy rejection sampler tries at most 64 candidates. Failure returns the wrapped mean. Non-finite mean becomes zero; negative/non-finite concentration becomes zero.

subsection:: Sampling limits

Concentration at or below 1e-8 uses a uniform circular draw. Above 1e6 a wrapped normal with standard deviation code::1/sqrt(kappa):: is an asymptotic approximation that avoids cancellation. This approximation has the same high-concentration limit; it is not an exact von Mises sampler. Outputs are radians in [-pi, pi); float endpoint rounding is kept inside that interval. No filtering or audio normalization is applied.

One sample is drawn at construction even when trig is zero, as in the other Stochastica distributions. A rising reset restores the seed and draws the first sample using current parameters; it wins over a simultaneous trigger. Values hold between edges. There is no warmup.

Like link::Classes/TRand:: it samples and holds on triggers, but it samples a circular distribution instead of a uniform interval.

subsection:: Process view

image::von-mises-circular.png#Polar sample histograms for concentration 0, 2, and 8. The wrap boundary is continuous.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: mean
Preferred direction in radians, wrapped to [-pi, pi); default 0.
argument:: kappa
Nonnegative circular concentration; default 1. Zero is uniform.
argument:: trig
A nonpositive-to-positive edge draws one sample. Held-positive triggers draw only once.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local PCG32 seed. Zero derives a seed from the parent Synth; nonzero is reproducible. Reset restores the original seed.
argument:: reset
Rising edge restores the original seed and samples once; takes priority over trig.
returns:: One angle in radians in [-pi, pi).

method:: kr
Control-rate version: one calculation spans the full control block. Event outputs last one block.

instancemethods::

examples::

subsection:: Circular values

Observe samples near a preferred direction.

code::
(
{ TVonMisesRand.kr(0, 6, Impulse.kr(4)).poll }.play
)
::

subsection:: Across the boundary

Angles on both sides of pi remain neighboring phases.

code::
(
{
    var event = Impulse.kr(5);
    var angle = TVonMisesRand.kr(pi - 0.1, 12, event);
    SinOsc.ar(330, angle, Decay2.kr(event, 0.005, 0.15) * 0.08)
}.play
)
::

subsection:: Circular spatial concentration

Four outputs form a ring. Angle divided by pi maps to PanAz position; use a four-channel output setup to hear the full ring.

code::
(
{
    var event = Impulse.kr(6);
    var angle = TVonMisesRand.kr(SinOsc.kr(0.03) * pi, 5, event);
    PanAz.ar(4, SinOsc.ar(700, 0, Decay2.kr(event, 0.002, 0.08) * 0.08), angle / pi)
}.play
)
::

